<title>CANADA: Canada oks C$20/tonne boost to CWB barley payment.</title>
<headline>Canada oks C$20/tonne boost to CWB barley payment.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's government Thursday approved a C$20/tonne increase to initial payments offered by Canadian Wheat Board to Prairie farmers for two-row malting barley and C$6/tonne for six-row malting barley, a CWB statement said.</p>
<p>The increase takes effect Feb 10, 1997, and will apply to deliveries made during the 1996/97 (Aug/July) marketing year.  </p>
<p>Initial payments are set and guaranteed by the Canadian government in time for the beginning of each crop year Aug 1.</p>
<p>It is a down payment estimated at between 70 to 80 percent of the expected world price during the coming marketing year.</p>
